1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Why are you doing this for me?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
I want you to go back to your landing castle, so you can find out where the real Princess of Salem is being held.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
But why would you trust me?

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Because I believe you want the same thing Princess of Salem does.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:22,000
There's one other thing I want you to find out for me.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Slain Troyart's objective. What's his plan?

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
His objective?

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Take this.

9
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:35,000
When you meet with the real Princess of Salem, give this to her.

10
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,000
She'll know you're among those on her side.

11
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Oh, my lady!

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,000
To be continued...

13
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:32,980
Thank you.

14
00:01:33,000 --> 00:02:02,980
Thank you.

15
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Thank you.

16
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Well done.

17
00:02:34,000 --> 00:03:04,000


18
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Thank you.

19
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,280
By combining Alt-Noah's power with Earth's resources, we will begin to build our world.

20
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,280
Thank you.

21
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:11,280
Thank you.

22
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,280
Thank you.

23
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:13,280
Thank you.

24
00:04:13,280 --> 00:04:15,280
Thank you.

25
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:18,080
Maybe Command thinks the odds are somehow on their side.

26
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:21,500
So then do you think those odds will extend to us as well?

27
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:23,120
I don't, ma'am.

28
00:04:23,720 --> 00:04:27,120
In that case, we may want to do some calculating of our own.

29
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,680
Well, some input would be nice.

30
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:34,120
Young Kaiska, that brain of yours got anything we can use against those Martians?

31
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:35,700
It's really tricky.

32
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:38,280
Electris uses lightning as a weapon.

33
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,320
Scandia turns invisible.

34
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,140
Both are formidable.

35
00:04:42,140 --> 00:04:47,200
As far as the Ortegia's duplicating ability, I'll need to get more data.

36
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:49,800
Lightning, invisible, and the cloner.

37
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:52,340
It's like we're stuck in a superhero film.

38
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:58,200
We know from our experience that when the Ortegia reproduces, it always splits from one into two.

39
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,820
It never multiplies into three or more.

40
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:05,160
And the new clone always appears within a radius of 30 meters.

41
00:05:05,380 --> 00:05:09,220
No matter how many times it splits, there's got to be only one living pilot, right?

42
00:05:09,460 --> 00:05:10,420
The rest are drones.

43
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:13,500
So then we've got to identify and destroy the original.

44
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,420
But how are we going to do that?

45
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:19,700
We put some kind of mark on the original and keep track of it after that.

46
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,480
And as for the other ones, we know we can use smoke to track Scandia's movements.

47
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:25,900
And the lightning one?

48
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,500
Any ideas there?

49
00:05:27,500 --> 00:05:32,400
We get hit by that one, it'll blow out our electronics and our control systems again.

50
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,960
Well, what about some insulation?

51
00:05:34,460 --> 00:05:35,780
That doesn't conduct electricity.

52
00:05:36,100 --> 00:05:36,480
Huh?

53
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:38,280
Any brains in that head?

54
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:40,360
What are you, a grade schooler?

55
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,400
What do you mean?

56
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:43,220
And what is so wrong with that idea?

57
00:05:43,620 --> 00:05:45,620
Air is already a very good insulator.

58
00:05:46,140 --> 00:05:50,680
There's no way to block a discharge powerful enough to punch through so much insulation.

59
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:52,860
I'll tell you what makes it really tricky.

60
00:05:53,240 --> 00:05:56,720
The fact that they've been teaming up instead of competing against each other.

61
00:05:56,720 --> 00:05:59,180
Yeah, they're bad enough just one at a time.

62
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:00,740
Now wait a minute.

63
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:02,920
I have an idea.

64
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:03,980
Your eye.

65
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,900
You're not going to use it now, are you?

66
00:06:06,460 --> 00:06:08,160
There's nothing to worry about, Inko.

67
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:08,780
It's alright.

68
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:09,560
Huh?

69
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:14,880
I always have a self-mutating code running, so it gets more and more optimized over time.

70
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:18,340
Its predictive ability is even more accurate now.

71
00:06:19,300 --> 00:06:21,480
Com, can you manage a loadout change for me?

72
00:06:21,720 --> 00:06:22,340
No problem.

73
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:23,540
Just tell me what you need.

74
00:06:23,540 --> 00:06:25,320
What I had in the space fight.

75
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:26,880
I need those.

76
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:37,680
Princess Lamrina, I thought you'd like to know.

77
00:06:38,080 --> 00:06:39,920
The Earth invasion is well in hand.

78
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:40,960
I see.

79
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,020
I knew you could do it, Slane.

80
00:06:43,220 --> 00:06:48,680
And perhaps, for morale, could you say a few words to the Orbital Knights who served so well in battle?

81
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:50,940
You mean that I should speak to them?

82
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:56,900
Yes, if Princess Asalem were to honor their achievements, more knights could be won over to our side.

83
00:06:57,920 --> 00:06:58,860
To our side?

84
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:00,920
Yes, Princess Lamrina.

85
00:07:02,700 --> 00:07:03,740
Very well, then.

86
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:08,020
Incidentally, Slane, what is my sister's current medical status?

87
00:07:08,620 --> 00:07:11,800
Unfortunately, the reports say she is still in critical condition.

88
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,020
I see.

89
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:17,240
For now, all we can do is maintain our faith in the medical staff.

90
00:07:17,700 --> 00:07:18,400
That is true.

91
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,860
Of course, we shall pray for a quick recovery.

92
00:07:21,420 --> 00:07:23,200
Try not to dwell on it, Slane.

93
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,660
I thank you, Your Highness.

94
00:07:25,200 --> 00:07:26,120
You're very kind.

95
00:07:26,900 --> 00:07:28,220
Now, please excuse me.

96
00:07:30,800 --> 00:07:31,980
You are a liar.

97
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:43,640
This is Clydesdale leader to all units.

98
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,800
Spread out and maintain distance.

99
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:48,520
Mustang leader to Mustang Zero-Zero.

100
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:50,460
Now, what's their position?

101
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,560
Preliminary data is in.

102
00:07:52,820 --> 00:07:54,340
Sending coordinates and velocity.

103
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:57,600
Mustang 1-1 and 2-2.

104
00:07:58,120 --> 00:07:58,940
Go, move out!

105
00:07:59,320 --> 00:07:59,760
Roger!

106
00:07:59,760 --> 00:08:13,900
Primary target is the Ortegium Master.

107
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,360
Let's get him boxed up.

108
00:08:15,640 --> 00:08:16,780
Take him down, now.

109
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:18,880
Saria platoon, straight ahead.

110
00:08:19,420 --> 00:08:21,420
Gauntlet platoon, flank him from the west.

111
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,260
Saria platoon, acknowledged.

112
00:08:23,480 --> 00:08:24,860
Gauntlet platoon, acknowledged.

113
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,040
Master identified on the right.

114
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,040
Third from the end.

115
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,180
Commence attack!

116
00:08:35,380 --> 00:08:37,680
Did you really think you had the original?

117
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:39,580
Well, guess again.

118
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:43,500
Aye, Count Olga will deal with this enemy force.

119
00:08:45,380 --> 00:08:47,060
Nonius platoon, Plevin platoon.

120
00:08:47,580 --> 00:08:49,200
Concentrate attack on the Scandia.

121
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:50,480
Let's take him out.

122
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:51,720
Fire smoke grenades!

123
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:59,280
Spotted him!

124
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:00,380
On my nine!

125
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:02,380
Fire! Fire! Fire!

126
00:09:04,940 --> 00:09:06,660
Using the same old tricks again.

127
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:08,520
You are very tedious, aren't you?

128
00:09:08,820 --> 00:09:10,340
What do you think we should do with them?

129
00:09:10,620 --> 00:09:11,900
Ideas, Count Zebrin?

130
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,640
Let us show them a little magic.

131
00:09:14,020 --> 00:09:15,220
Shall we, Countess Raffia?

132
00:09:19,720 --> 00:09:21,300
The smoke screen just vanished.

133
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:24,860
Smoke is a colloid, and ionization settles it out.

134
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,020
But here is another way to use.

135
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,560
The power of lightning.

136
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,940
Lightning attack from invisibility?

137
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:36,180
When one is defeated in a battle,

138
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:38,780
shouldn't it be a beautiful death?

139
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:42,720
Assuming you are a true cataphract pilot.

140
00:09:43,400 --> 00:09:43,740
Captain!

141
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:46,780
Both the main force and our assault units are running into trouble!

142
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:48,640
That's what I was afraid of.

143
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,840
Invisible and Lightning are now a team.

144
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,600
Mustang Zero Zero, what's your status?

145
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:54,800
I've got the data.

146
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:59,480
Smoke screen negation and expanded invisibility field were unexpected, though.

147
00:09:59,720 --> 00:10:00,720
Can you make an adjustment?

148
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,260
I have to.

149
00:10:02,260 --> 00:10:09,700
So then, this war has been going on for almost two years now, while I was unconscious?

150
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:11,280
Yes.

151
00:10:12,280 --> 00:10:13,440
And it is slain?

152
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:13,940
Who...

153
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:16,440
What has been going on?

154
00:10:16,780 --> 00:10:18,080
I don't understand.

155
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:21,360
Milady!

156
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:22,680
Where are you going?

157
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:25,000
I'm going to see slain.

158
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:27,640
To learn the truth behind all this.

159
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:28,820
But, Milady!

160
00:10:35,820 --> 00:10:37,520
Wait, who are...

161
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:38,780
Tell me why.

162
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:45,640
Why must you always stand in my way?

163
00:10:46,640 --> 00:10:47,920
But who are you?

164
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:49,420
Who am I?

165
00:10:49,420 --> 00:10:51,560
I am you, of course.

166
00:10:51,560 --> 00:11:05,660
Using a tactical data link for multidimensional analysis of enemy behavior to deduce the enemy's battle habits,

167
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:10,880
We will deploy friendlies in positions vulnerable to the enemy's preferred attack patterns,

168
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:13,260
then prompt them to engage.

169
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:17,280
But will the analysis be complete in time?

170
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:19,180
Sending most recent data.

171
00:11:19,460 --> 00:11:20,220
Take your positions.

172
00:11:20,780 --> 00:11:21,080
Roger.

173
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:22,780
Roger from over here, too.

174
00:11:22,780 --> 00:11:29,600
The probability is he's right-handed.

175
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:33,180
He moves counterclockwise to attack enemies on his left.

176
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,740
I don't care much for being bait.

177
00:11:38,380 --> 00:11:39,140
Where is he now?

178
00:11:39,980 --> 00:11:41,640
He's circling around behind you.

179
00:11:42,220 --> 00:11:45,920
To keep from giving away his position, he'll hold off on his lightning attack.

180
00:11:46,280 --> 00:11:50,160
Then, once behind his target, he'll come to a quick stop and take aim.

181
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:54,060
Yuki, now!

182
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:55,180
Is he really there?

183
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:01,500
Found him!

184
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:02,460
What was that?

185
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:03,820
This is Mustang Leader.

186
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:04,980
We have the target spotted.

187
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,440
Mustang Zero-Zero, launching.

188
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:08,320
Roger that.

189
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:10,340
Mustang Zero-Zero, go drop!

190
00:12:20,160 --> 00:12:21,520
This Scandia's leg.

191
00:12:21,920 --> 00:12:24,440
It can't support the extra weight of Electris.

192
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:25,740
Disconnect the link.

193
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:27,040
I will handle it.

194
00:12:27,340 --> 00:12:27,820
Get clear.

195
00:12:29,160 --> 00:12:30,260
Targets confirmed.

196
00:12:31,100 --> 00:12:31,900
Firing anchors.

197
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:42,000
You know that will not work.

198
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:43,720
And what about these rounds?

199
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:48,620
How can you...

200
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:50,600
Lightning flows from high potential to low.

201
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:54,200
It won't strike an object with the same electrical potential.

202
00:12:54,880 --> 00:12:56,840
That's what keeps you from striking yourself.

203
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:01,440
Take this!

204
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:03,900
It's too late.

205
00:13:04,280 --> 00:13:05,960
The cables gave us the same potential.

206
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,180
Come stop you now.

207
00:13:07,340 --> 00:13:09,900
It cannot be.

208
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:12,320
Is this that orange one I've heard about?

209
00:13:12,320 --> 00:13:15,080
Count Zebrin, no!

210
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:16,760
I'm sending you help.

211
00:13:17,060 --> 00:13:17,880
Just hold on.

212
00:13:22,860 --> 00:13:24,000
No, Inoho!

213
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,360
Smoke grenades!

214
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:31,540
There you are.

215
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:32,380
Fire!

216
00:13:41,100 --> 00:13:41,940
Curse you.

217
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:44,240
You murdered my noble comrades.

218
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:45,480
I will avenge them.

219
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:56,880
Now, are you okay?

220
00:13:57,880 --> 00:13:59,000
Yes, thanks, Yuki.

221
00:13:59,560 --> 00:14:00,460
On your nine!

222
00:14:00,460 --> 00:14:05,580
Cause it's time to wake you up.

223
00:14:11,300 --> 00:14:12,380
Here they come!

224
00:14:13,040 --> 00:14:13,840
Fire and will!

225
00:14:13,840 --> 00:14:36,260
You wish to see me, Princess Lemrina?

226
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:38,880
Yes, Slane.

227
00:14:39,520 --> 00:14:41,140
What do you think you're up to?

228
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:49,500
About Princess Asalem. My sister. She has actually awakened, hasn't she?

229
00:14:52,340 --> 00:14:56,080
I knew that I would have to tell you eventually.

230
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,120
I think it's time you explained yourself.

231
00:15:00,020 --> 00:15:03,760
Unfortunately, Princess Asalem is not quite herself yet.

232
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:13,280
I need you to portray her still, just for the time being, until her health improves and she has had a chance to recover, in order for us to create a new world.

233
00:15:13,840 --> 00:15:15,840
To create a new world?

234
00:15:16,320 --> 00:15:24,700
Yes. A world that is free of worry. A world of everlasting peace, that is without conflict and without sadness.

235
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:27,680
And who do you have in mind to rule this world?

236
00:15:28,040 --> 00:15:31,860
Her Highness. Asalem vs. Alucia, of course.

237
00:15:31,860 --> 00:15:36,020
Do you think that she even wants such a thing?

238
00:15:36,340 --> 00:15:42,340
I know for a fact she does not. Which is the reason why it has to be presented to her.

239
00:15:42,340 --> 00:15:51,960
Your Highness, do you know why it is that wars break out?

240
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:56,440
Wars are a means of negotiation between states.

241
00:15:56,680 --> 00:16:01,460
Not quite. Wars always break out because there is someone there to fight against.

242
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:09,920
There are two options to eliminate war. Invade and assimilate, or exterminate your adversary so that only you remain.

243
00:16:10,860 --> 00:16:14,480
The history of mankind is the history of conflict.

244
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:20,540
At the very instant Mars split off from Earth, war became an utter inevitability.

245
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:28,680
It's true. If I had not started this war, eventually, someone else would have.

246
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:32,760
You're not the same. Something has changed in you.

247
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:39,940
No. You are no longer the gentle slain I once knew, are you?

248
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:54,560
No. Princess Asalem.

249
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,500
I told her everything.

250
00:17:01,500 --> 00:17:06,800
In the name of the Verse Empire, Asalem vs. Alucia, Royal Princess.

251
00:17:06,800 --> 00:17:13,800
Hereby orders Count Slain Sosbaum Troyard to immediately cease hostilities.

252
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,620
I thought getting the Master would bring this to an end.

253
00:17:23,260 --> 00:17:24,680
But which is the real one?

254
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:27,580
Obviously, the one we marked wasn't the original.

255
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:29,480
Where's that bastard hiding?

256
00:17:29,600 --> 00:17:33,660
I assumed that one of these guys would be the original, but it may actually be incorrect.

257
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:35,100
Inaho, what do you mean?

258
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:38,100
In analyzing the duplicates, I learned something interesting.

259
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:44,880
At the instant they manifest, the Master's state is perfectly duplicated, from orientation to energy level.

260
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:46,400
And that means what?

261
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:50,880
I believe he's using quantum teleportation to manufacture these copies.

262
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:56,440
Except the original is left intact instead of being destroyed, creating a perfect duplicate.

263
00:17:56,980 --> 00:17:58,660
Again? What the hell does that mean?

264
00:17:58,800 --> 00:18:00,100
What it means is...

265
00:18:00,780 --> 00:18:01,120
Hmm.

266
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:04,080
That they are all the real one.

267
00:18:08,820 --> 00:18:11,760
Slave all of the cataphract platoons into my fire controls.

268
00:18:11,900 --> 00:18:13,820
Send request to company command post.

269
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:14,420
Yes, ma'am.

270
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:17,280
Locating all Ortegeus.

271
00:18:17,860 --> 00:18:18,980
Their vectors and coordinates.

272
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:20,800
How many more is he gonna make?

273
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:22,760
Right now would be good, young Kaizuka.

274
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:24,280
Target numbers increasing.

275
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:26,380
I need to update my data.

276
00:18:27,060 --> 00:18:28,560
Do what you gotta do, but quick!

277
00:18:29,040 --> 00:18:30,520
Our ammo isn't gonna last forever!

278
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:33,380
Tactical data linking completed.

279
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:38,020
Slave all UFV cataphract aiming systems to my control.

280
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:40,920
Now, how much longer?

281
00:18:41,640 --> 00:18:43,200
We have one chance.

282
00:18:43,780 --> 00:18:45,280
If they're all real...

283
00:18:45,980 --> 00:18:50,260
All targets now locked.

284
00:18:50,860 --> 00:18:51,260
Fire!

285
00:18:51,260 --> 00:19:11,360
Oh, wow.

286
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:17,560
Every one of them was real, so they all had to be taken care of at once.

287
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:20,180
Enemy cataphracts totally eliminated!

288
00:19:20,180 --> 00:19:22,260
Wow, you did it, Inahal!

289
00:19:22,700 --> 00:19:23,160
Mm-hmm.

290
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:24,820
I'm just glad that it worked.

291
00:19:25,440 --> 00:19:26,460
Thanks for all your help.

292
00:19:32,300 --> 00:19:32,840
Slain.

293
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,780
Please, you have to end this madness.

294
00:19:39,180 --> 00:19:40,280
Princess Asalem.

295
00:19:41,740 --> 00:19:44,180
I'm afraid I cannot obey your order.

296
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:45,560
For you see,

297
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:49,780
I am no longer a citizen of the Verse Empire.

298
00:19:51,620 --> 00:19:52,940
I'm truly sorry.

299
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:56,020
But I must take you all into custody.

300
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:59,200
Captain, a message from General Headquarters.

301
00:19:59,760 --> 00:20:03,820
Sorry, you'll only have about two minutes before the comm satellite dips below the line of sight, ma'am.

302
00:20:03,820 --> 00:20:05,700
I hope that'll be enough.

303
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,140
Put it on speaker, if you would.

304
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:09,780
Deucalion here.

305
00:20:10,340 --> 00:20:11,560
Captain Mogberech speaking.

306
00:20:12,480 --> 00:20:14,120
This is Vice Admiral Aelis Hokinen.

307
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:16,180
That was a brilliant operation, Captain.

308
00:20:16,620 --> 00:20:18,400
What is your status on the upgrades?

309
00:20:18,660 --> 00:20:19,740
Almost finished, sir.

310
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:21,800
I am very pleased to hear it.

311
00:20:22,080 --> 00:20:25,220
The Deucalion will need this equipment on her next mission.

312
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:27,560
Will we be going to the satellite belt?

313
00:20:28,040 --> 00:20:28,620
Is that it?

314
00:20:29,020 --> 00:20:29,400
No.

315
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:31,180
It'll be higher this time.

316
00:20:32,360 --> 00:20:33,920
You will be breathed later.

317
00:20:35,260 --> 00:20:36,200
Connection is broken.

318
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:38,620
The laser link gain is starting to fade.

319
00:20:39,380 --> 00:20:41,340
Comm satellite now leaving line of sight.

320
00:20:41,760 --> 00:20:43,600
I guess he didn't want to hear me say no.

321
00:20:44,140 --> 00:20:46,260
Sounds like we could be in for a large battle.

322
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:47,240
Damn it all.

323
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:52,460
He thinks he can put us into play any way he wants, because we have Alt-Noah.

324
00:20:53,300 --> 00:20:55,400
So then it's a space loadout, ma'am?

325
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:57,600
A catapult module, too.

326
00:21:04,820 --> 00:21:05,920
My Lord Slane.

327
00:21:06,240 --> 00:21:06,900
What is it?

328
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:09,660
The princesses are comfortably settled in their quarters.

329
00:21:10,420 --> 00:21:11,020
Thank you.

330
00:21:11,580 --> 00:21:13,040
My Lord, you had to do this.

331
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:16,260
Even if they don't understand now, one day they...

332
00:21:16,260 --> 00:21:16,780
No matter.

333
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:19,820
Whether they understand or not is irrelevant.

334
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:23,740
My Lord Count, a spaceship is on approach to the base.

335
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:25,720
